Here is the root cause:
core0" in `TestSolrProperties` was likely caused by the test environment not correctly referencing the Solr core configuration file (`solr.xml`). This could happen if the test was using a default or incorrect `solr.xml` file instead of a test-specific one, leading to the absence of the expected core definition during the test execution. The modifications in the patch address this by ensuring that a proper test configuration file (`test-solr.xml`) is used, which contains the necessary core definitions.

